              The cash machine. Record earnings, record returns. Twenty-six consecutive years of dividend increases — and the buyback is accelerating.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="reveal">
            <img
              src={lng.src}
              width={PLATE_W}
              height={lngH}
              alt="A printed economics breakdown showing the LNG chain from Montney wellhead to Asian delivery, with cost and price at each stage."
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <figcaption>
              From wellhead to tanker. The spread between C$2.10 in the field and US$12+ at the port is the margin that justifies the entire pipeline.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="reveal">Five layers, and they don't move together</h2>
        <p class="body reveal">
          "Energy stock" covers five different businesses. Which layer a company sits in decides what an oil price move, a pipeline expansion, or a contract signing does to it. Establish that first.
        </p>

        <div class="tbl-scroll reveal">
          <table class="deal-tbl">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Layer</th>
                <th>What it actually earns</th>
                <th>What we watch next</th>
